  abstract = {Finite-precision errors can break the zero-sum constraint of cross-entropy gradients. The resulting drift creates a feedback loop between classifier and feature means, termed Numerical Feature Inflation. This offers a numerical explanation for rapid norm growth and Slingshot loss spikes, while also predicting that parameter growth can occur without visible spikes.}
